+---
+id: task-003-give-back-single-use-coupon-on-cancel-free-shipping-at-50-euro
+type: task
+title: "Give back single-use coupon on cancel; free shipping at 50 euro"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+# Request
+
+Two reports on the order service.
+
+1. Paolo: placed an order with his one-time welcome code, cancelled it the same day, and the code was
+   then refused as already used. Cause: `Orders.cancel` gave the coupon back under the customer's name
+   instead of the order id, so the single-use record was never released. Fixed in `src/orders.ts`.
+2. Support: €4.90 shipping charged on goods of exactly €50.00. The README says free from €50.00 after
+   discounts, before VAT. The current code already does this (`>=` threshold, fixed under task-001); I
+   could not reproduce the report on it, so no code change. The order was probably placed before that
+   fix. A regression test through `quote` pins the behaviour.
+
+Tests added to `test/regressions.test.ts`; `npm test` passes (21 tests).
